ADDENDA <Act No. 16602, Nov. 26, 2019>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force three months after the date of its promulgation; provided, Articles 2 through 4, 6, and 7 of the Addenda shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparation for establishment of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources)
(1) The Minister of Environment shall constitute the Establishment Committee of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources Center (hereinafter referred to as the "Establishment Committee") within one month from the date of promulgation of this Act to handle the affairs necessary for the establishment of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources.
(2) The Establishment Committee shall be comprised of not more than ten members appointed or commissioned by the Minister of Environment, including the chairperson, and the chairperson shall be the Vice Minister of Environment.
(3) The Establishment Committee shall prepare the Articles of incorporation, obtain approval thereof from the Minister of Environment, and complete registration for incorporation of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources by the date this Act enters into force.
(4) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 8, the Minister of Environment shall appoint the first executive officers of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources appointed after this Act enters into force, from among several persons recommended by the Establishment Committee.
(5) The Establishment Committee shall without delay transfer its business affairs to the head of the president after filing for registration for incorporation of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources and the Establishment Committee shall be deemed dissolved and the members shall be deemed decommissioned.
Article 3 (Incorporation expenses)
The costs and expenses incurred in the establishment of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources shall be borne by the State.
Article 4 (Granting concessions for goods without consideration)
Notwithstanding the provisions of the Commodity Management Act and the Cultural Heritage Protection Act, the State may gratuitously transfer goods and cultural heritage (limited to cultural heritage designated as endangered wildlife under the Wildlife Protection and Management Act) managed by the livelihood resource conservation agency establishment promotion planning team (hereinafter referred to as "establishment promotion planning team") prescribed in Article 59 of the Act on the Organization of the Ministry of Environment before this Act enters into force to the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources; provided, goods shall be subject to prior consultation with the Minister of Economy and Finance.
Article 5 (Succession to rights and obligations)
(1) The Honam National Institute of Biological Resources established pursuant to this Act comprehensively inherits the rights and obligations of the Establishment Promotion Planning Team.
(2) The name of the Establishment Promotion Planning Team indicated in the register or other public record with respect to the rights and obligations that the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources comprehensively inherits pursuant to paragraph (1) shall be deemed the name of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources.
Article 6 (Special cases concerning preparation and submission of budget planning)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 22(1), the Establishment Committee may prepare and submit a budget bill of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources in the first business year which begins after the establishment of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning budget)
(1) The Honam National Institute of Biological Resources may implement the budget under the jurisdiction of the previous Establishment Promotion Planning Team according to the previous examples until the budget of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources is determined.
(2) The budget executed pursuant to paragraph (1) shall be deemed to have been executed in accordance with the determined budget when the budget of the Honam National Institute of Biological Resources is confirmed.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning National Institute of Biological Resources)
Any National Institute of Biological Resources established under Article 39 of the former Wildlife Protection and Management Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a National Institute of Biological Resources established under this Act.
Article 9 Omitted.
Article 10 (Relationships to other statutes or regulations)
A citation of a provision of the previous Act on the Establishment and Management of National Institute of Nakdong River Biological Resources by any other statute or regulation as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a citation of the corresponding provisions in this Act in lieu of the previous provisions, if such corresponding provisions exist in this Act.

